# Frozen artefacts: byte-exact, never line-ending-converted.
# core.autocrlf=true on Windows would rewrite these on checkout and break every
# declared SHA-256, including for the person who wrote them.
#
# The catch-all below is deliberate. An earlier version of this file listed
# extensions only, and silently missed LICENSE: it has no extension, so no
# *.ext pattern matched it. A clean clone rewrote it to CRLF and its declared
# digest failed -- 28/29 instead of 29/29. Matching every path means a new
# artefact cannot be missed by omission rather than by decision.
*               -text

# Kept explicit so the intent survives if the catch-all is ever narrowed.
LICENSE         -text
*.md            -text
*.ipynb         -text
*.json          -text
*.jsonl         -text
*.csv           -text
*.txt           -text
*.xlsx          binary
